{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002145-having-a-job-while-adventuring","id":1002145,"title":"Having a job while adventuring","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-12T00:31:19-08:00","id":1002145,"title":"Having a job while adventuring","content":"Not every hero has a very low need for sleep like Bruce Wayne or Buffy Summers. Or is independently wealthy like Bilbo Baggins. Or has Hermione to do all their homework like the kids in Harry Potter who aren't Hermione.<br /> <br /> Besides those options, what are some good ways a player character can earn their Resources while still having the flexibility to take off a few weeks to infiltrate a Technocracy Construct/steal roc eggs in the Dreaming/claw a long succession of Wyrm creatures to death?<br /> <br /> Maybe they're professors and they only adventure in the summer. Or they're artists and, like, sell topaz jewelry or something (Resources 1 at best). I'd be curious to know what proportion of Awakened beings have a trust fund or inheritance. Is unearned wealth the most common superpower in the World of Darkness? Being a small business owner is kind of plausible if you can buy that you can make enough money while taking all that time off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 11-12-2016, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T01:20:51-08:00","id":1002153,"title":"","content":"A lot of supernaturals rely on support supernaturals for help. Ghouls, and kinfolk are probably the most direct examples because of the practical difficulties for vampires and werewolves holding down day jobs.<br /> <br /> The Internet is also a major boon for this sort of thing. A vampire can use the Internet to be a &quot;day trader&quot; in foreign markets instead of domestic ones, and with a smart phone can be working the markets pretty much anywhere. There are lots of ways to sell more as an artist via the Internet, and lots of supernaturals can actually profit off of art in ways normal humans can't; also helps avoid direct contact with normal humans and such.<br /> <br /> Any sort of freelance or by-contract style job is also an option, because you can simply not take jobs while you're busy with your other stuff. Obviously most such work isn't super profitable, but there are people that can command $200K for a single speech (obviously there's a lot that you need to be able to back that up, but it does happen). This can also work within your supernatural group so that others can handle the difficulty of avoiding mortal authorities (basically the Assamite MO in Cam territories is to be mercenaries for them); a lot of mages - esp. Technocrats - probably work for other mages would understand the demands on their time.<br /> <br /> Setting and era also matter a lot. Vampires far from the Sabbat/Camarilla fight who are mostly focused on local politics have lots of reasons to be actively involved in local businesses to their own personal benefit (even if they leave &quot;ownership&quot; to ghouls), while vampires on the front of Sect warfare are going to be concerned with instability and want less tangible assets. The 2e era of most of the games has a lot more focus on running around adventuring, which poses more problems for having a wider range of jobs, while the Revised era of the games largely expects a more local focus which makes it easier to justify holding down a regular job along with your supernatural stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T07:58:46-08:00","id":1002218,"title":"","content":"Some of it depends on how much time passes between &quot;Adventures&quot;. If the characters are embroiled in one event after the next in rapid succession, it monopolizes their time. Conversely, a more seasonal Chronicle - where character have a lot of down time to pursue their own affairs - can make it so their adventures only happen every so often. This is especially true for player-driven plots, where the PCs themselves determine where they go and what they do. A Mage who holds down a day job can schedule their trip to the Umbra or to an isolated South American temple for when the character has vacation days.<br /> <br /> Then you have the Technocrats, for whom busting Reality Deviants <i>is</i> their job.<br /> <br /> Or how about Mages who use Matter or Life to create valuable goods and services. The whole lead to gold angle can attract a lot of unwanted attention, but less visible materials like copper wire or helium can still provide a Mage with steady income. Or the Life Mage who is commissioned by other Mages or Sleepers in-the-know, to provide healing, cosmetic alterations, and youth restoring agents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T19:22:46-08:00","id":1004757,"title":"","content":"I wonder how do Kinfolk give money for the septs upkeep do they donate it some fund, or come every month with a check. could cause trouble with the SAD if theirs an investigation into such a supposed &quot;charity&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T21:02:26-08:00","id":1004791,"title":"","content":"Unless it's particularly large sums of money, they probably don't give the money to the Sept over spending it for the Sept by going out and buying whatever the Sept needs.<br /> <br /> A charity is most likely going to orient around something that's part of the Sept's stuff. If the Sept's protectorate contains a non-profit wolf sanctuary, it's probably run by kin, and relies on kin donates for the majority of the money. Nobody's going to question them using a lot of that money for things like buying deer from local hunters (which can be kin or Garou) to feed the wolves there.<br /> <br /> There's only something to investigate if the charity is spending money in large sums on stuff that doesn't make sense for a charity of its type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T04:10:32-08:00","id":1004869,"title":"","content":"I got the impression from Kinfolk Breed apart, and unsung heroes alike, that many garou derive resources from Kenning kinfolk that host them, or patronize them.<br /> <br /> Oh a few years ago I came up with a hypothetical idea for a charity, how would this work out.<br /> <br /> &quot;My charity helps ex convicts move on with their lives. 80% of the money we have goes to one congressmans campaign fund.&quot;<br /> <br /> think that could prosecuted for fraud?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}